PREPnet Acceptable Use Policy and Agreement

Purpose
The purpose of PREPnet is to enhance and support research and educational 
activities, and to foster economic development within Pennsylvania
by providing and promoting high speed data communications facilities
and services.

Acceptable Use
Acceptable uses of PREPnet include, but are not limited to, the following:
- Use for purposes of, or in support of, educaiton and research.
- Use for purposes of technology transfer or the economic development
  of Pennsylvania.
- Traffic must originate or terminate at a PREPnet member or affiliate 
  organization.
- Traffic exiting PREPnet to the NSFNET backbone or other networks
  to which PREPnet may be connected is governed by the policies of 
  those networks. (Attached is a copy of the NSFNET Acceptable Use Policy)

Unacceptable Use
- Use of PREPnet for illegal purposes or for unauthorized access to 
  systems, software or data.
- Activities that interfere with the ability of others to effectively
  use PREPnet or other facilities connected to the network.
- Commercial usage that does not meet the above criterial for
acceptability.

Conditions
- Violations of this policy may result in the expulsion of the member or
  affiliate from PREPnet, termination of PREPnet services, and forfiture
  of all fees paid to date.
- Questions related to acceptable use should be directed to the PREPnet
  Network Information Center.

Agreement
I understand and agree to abide by this PREPnet Acceptable Use Policy.

