NFS != Internet.  (I know Carl knows it.)

There is no legal entity called the Internet.  Therefore there is no
Internet policy.  As the name implies, Internet is an interconnection
of various networks that agree to (or gateway between) a set of
network protocols.  Parts of it are owned by national governments
(yes, plural), state governments, commercial businesses, non-profit
entities, etc.  Not all have AUPs.  And the distinct AUPs differ.

