that if a user complains about the display of another user, the second user
will be ordered to remove it regardless of content, and without any
investigation. I don't believe that you intend this to be the policy. Will
you admins really order a student to terminate a program if another student
is offended by it's output? You policy says that the admin will do so
immediately without regard for content. Again, I suspect that you won't
actually do this, but rather want the policy in place to refer to when a
problem occurs.

  Neither the current policy nor the draconian one are particularly simple.
A more simple policy would be to refer to you university policy for
harassment.

