[From a private college.]

Perhaps we are an unusual site because we get very few complaints about what
our users post.  Partly because of this we have no formal policy on news
complaints so decisions are made based upon the overall system usage policy
and, more remotely, on the [XXX] Honor Code.  Thus I can't
give you an exact response as to how such things are handled, but I can
provide a brief descrition of what the overall process would be like.

First we (we=system staff + intern + overall administrator) determine if
this is something we feel should be dealt with.  We have no desire to censor
posters merely because someone (even ourselves) finds the views offensive.
However there are activities, such as harassment, that grossly violate the
rights/dignity of the individual that we do not find acceptable.

Next we investigate, which would include listening in on the news group
involved and talking to the person accused if possible.  Often other
individuals beyond the initiator of the complaint are involved and we would
solicit their views also.

Based on the investigation we decide on the appropriate action to take.  The
student is informed of this and his/her right to meet with a review committee
to reconsider the decision.
