: One persons' erotica or casual fiction is another persons' harassment.

Is the solution therefore to restrict all speech that anyone might consider
to constitute harrassment?  Somehow this doesn't seem right.  

There is a real dilemma for universities that I don't know how to resolve.
On the one hand, universities have a special role to play in our society as
bastions of free speech and free expression generally.  Universities must
stand ready to protect speech that is unpopular, whatever the reason for
its unpopularity.  On the other hand, universities, especially those that 
accept public funding, seem to have a responsibility to protect their members
from intimidation, and some forms of harassment probably constitute intimida-
tion.



